+# Frontier — S5-CLM-00003490
+
+ANCHOR:RES-00 identifies the frozen crystal-uniqueness object and its Stage6
+alias. ANCHOR:RES-01 is the exact Iff.rfl transport in Statement.lean.
+ANCHOR:RES-02 records a deterministic finite exploration, and
+ANCHOR:RES-03 classifies what remains open.
+
+## Exact orientation
+
+The orientation is Claim:
+
+∀ n a b c d, IsCrystalWithComponents n a b →
+  IsCrystalWithComponents n c d →
+  ({a, b} : Finset ℕ) = {c, d}
+
+## Typed frontier
+
+- F-PROOF (proof): prove the equality for arbitrary n,a,b,c,d and both
+  crystal hypotheses. The missing cut is a complete mathematical uniqueness
+  argument.
+- F-REFUTE (refutation): exhibit a crystal with two inequivalent component
+  pairs and check every source hypothesis. No such checked witness is present.
+- F-COMPUTE (exploration): enumerate 2 ≤ a ≤ b ≤ 100; this is complete only
+  for that finite box and has no universal force.
+- F-LEAN (machine): close the exact-polarity root in Lean, either with a proof
+  of Target or a proof of Not Target.
+
+Finite searches cannot discharge a universal theorem, and the source sorryAx
+body is not an oracle. Mapping, human-resolution, and machine-root cut sets
+remain empty as required for an open handoff.
